    "done_when": "The report at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/snapshot-tests-under-load.html records, for each id and each revision, the failure count over 30 loops of that file under pytest -n 8 beside a CPU load generator, with each loop's log path. It names the cause of each failure with the evidence that shows it, such as a thread dump, a lock owner or a timestamp trace, states whether the joined_watch_sweeps fixture is implicated, and proposes the write paths and done-when of the fixing node. Each loop runs in a temporary RECKON_HOME with its basetemp under the run's own scratch directory, and the whole investigation stays inside a 50 minute budget.",
